&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in &lt;strong&gt;PayPay India&lt;/strong&gt; and focuses on technical program management across PayPay&#39;s product and platform portfolio. You will drive programs spanning payment processing, regulatory compliance, and platform integrations. The role requires close collaboration with India-based engineering teams and stakeholders across PayPay&#39;s headquarters in Japan.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;MAIN RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Program Execution &amp;amp; Delivery&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently drive technical programs of varying complexity, from well-defined projects to programs with multiple dependencies and cross-functional impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain program governance: risk registers, dependency maps, milestone tracking, and status reporting aligned to PayPay KPI framework (Predictability, Governance, Technical Health, Architecture).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor program health across progress, risks, blockers, and timelines. Communicate transparently with stakeholders and escalate proactively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make program-level decisions on scope, schedule, and trade-offs with increasing autonomy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Technical &amp;amp; Product Engagement&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to and influence technical design discussions, architecture reviews, and TDD (Technical Design Document) reviews with focus on security, compliance, and payment integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with AI/ML applications in FinTech (fraud detection, risk scoring, recommendation engines) as they relate to program scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure completion of non-functional requirements (Security, Performance, Compliance, Regulatory Requirements) prior to release milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering Managers and Product Managers to translate business goals into actionable execution plans aligned with financial services standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Agile &amp;amp; Process Leadership&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion Agile methodologies (Scrum, Kanban) within assigned teams, fostering transparency, collaboration, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tailor PayPay SDLC practices to team context while maintaining alignment with organizational standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate planning, retrospectives, and cross-team coordination meetings as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage generative AI tools appropriately to enhance productivity in documentation, analysis, and communication tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and drive process improvements that benefit program delivery and team effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Stakeholder Management &amp;amp; Communication&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage stakeholder alignment across Engineering, Product, Design, QA, and business partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong working relationships across teams and geographies (India, Japan headquarters).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent programs in leadership forums and cross-functional planning sessions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Mentorship &amp;amp; Collaboration&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor junior TPMs and new team members on program management fundamentals, PayPay processes, and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the TPM community knowledge base and process documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster an inclusive, collaborative environment within programs and teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or related technical field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years professional experience, including 5–7 years in technical program management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in FinTech, payments, banking, or financial services with exposure to payment processing or regulated product development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of software architecture, payment systems, and SDLC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience managing complex technical programs with multiple dependencies and cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of security and compliance requirements in financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical use of generative AI tools (ChatGPT, Claude, Copilot) for program management productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Agile methodologies (Scrum, Kanban)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of security and compliance frameworks in financial services (e.g., data protection, transaction security, regulatory standards)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing third-party integrations (payment gateways, banking systems, settlement platforms)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing AI/ML-driven programs in FinTech (fraud detection, risk models, transaction monitoring) with ability to identify AI-specific risks (data quality, model drift, bias, explainability)&lt;/li&gt;
