&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PayPay India is seeking an autonomous &lt;strong&gt;Senior Product Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to own and drive critical credit and merchant financial products in close collaboration with PayPay group companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will lead end-to-end product execution, turning business requirements into scalable platform features and seamless end-user experiences. You will work independently on day-to-day execution while collaborating closely with business partners, credit modeling experts, data teams, and engineering to deliver high-impact financial products in Japan.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Main Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Ownership &amp;amp; Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive end-to-end product lifecycle for merchant credit and bank integration products from ideation to launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Entity Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the key product owner working independently with business teams, partner banks, and PayPay group companies in Japan to understand business needs and translate them into actionable product roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Specifications &amp;amp; Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Write clear, high-quality PRDs and partner closely with engineering and UI/UX teams to build scalable platform capabilities and clean user experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Alignment with Modeling Teams:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with credit modeling, risk, and analytics teams to seamlessly incorporate scoring models, data pipelines, and decision engines into product flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data-Driven Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt; Analyze product performance, user behavior, and platform metrics using SQL and analytical tools to continuously identify feature gaps and optimize customer experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Roadmap Prioritization:&lt;/strong&gt; Define product challenges and opportunities, balancing speed of execution with long-term platform scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Minimum &lt;strong&gt;5+ years&lt;/strong&gt; of Product Management experience (7-9 years of overall experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical &amp;amp; Analytical Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor’s degree in a technology discipline (or 2+ years in a technical role) with a solid understanding of APIs, technical system architecture, statistical concepts, and data analysis (SQL).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Execution Autonomy:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong bias for action (&quot;Get Things Done&quot; attitude) with a track record of driving complex initiatives independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated success collaborating with cross-functional and international business stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain Versatility:&lt;/strong&gt; Prior background across fintech, e-commerce, consumer internet, or high-scale platform products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating with cross-border business teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leveraging AI/LLM tools in daily workflows (e.g., documentation, spec drafting, review, user flow mapping) while maintaining accountability for output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leverage AI/LLM-based tools in daily workflows (e.g., code development, reviews, testing, debugging, documentation), while ensuring human oversight, judgment, and accountability drive the final product.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
